{
  "language": "python",
  "layer": "normalization",
  "note": "Syntactic (form) oracle for Python -- keyed by ast node type. Same three buckets as the C profile: normalized (canonical handling), lowered (desugared surface form), opaque (known blind spot). Anything encountered outside all three is counted 'unnormalized'. Pure data; the front-end applies it.",
